# Native Workspace disclosures

Workspace options, Studio Administration and Atlas modality-link help use the
same Escape-to-close behaviour as the existing CT/MRI information panels.
`NativeDisclosure` renders one native `details` element: it adds no visual
controls, wrapper, storage, network request or navigation interception.

Escape closes only the connected, open, innermost disclosure and focuses its own
summary without scrolling. An already handled event or IME composition is left
alone. Caller keyboard handling runs first. Native Enter, Space and Tab behaviour
is retained; links keep their ordinary click and modifier semantics.

Closing does not unmount children, clear fields, submit a form, save a draft,
approve a review or discard unsaved edits. Source role checks, independent
entitlements, routes and initial Studio administration-open conditions are
unchanged. The existing head-disclosure utility is reused without changing it.

Synthetic DOM/SSR and isolated browser checks are engineering evidence, not
real-role, assistive-technology, clinical or release acceptance. The normal
owner preview remains unchanged until a separately authorized cutover.
